WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.486
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:10.610
I want to share with you today a story
about Israelis and Palestinian,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.596
but it's not about war and
it's not about conflict.

00:00:14.596 --> 00:00:21.533
It's a story of the technology bridge that
we're building between the two people.

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:25.327
So the story starts on
an aeroplane in 2017,

00:00:25.327 --> 00:00:30.703
I opened my eyes just as the pilot
announced our descent onto Israel.

00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:35.725
I could see the Aviv Skyline shining
brightly in the distance and

00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:38.608
can make out the logos of Facebook and

00:00:38.608 --> 00:00:44.007
Google wicks in ways plastered on
the facades of the high rises home.

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:48.357
But this time, I was going as part of
a delegation from Washington there to

00:00:48.357 --> 00:00:51.809
observe different policy trends and
shifting dynamics.

00:00:54.723 --> 00:00:58.077
Looking at my home through
a fresh set of eyes,

00:00:58.077 --> 00:01:03.152
I was amazed by the technology boom
that my country was experiencing.

00:01:03.152 --> 00:01:08.525
With over 7,000 startups,
400 multinationals, and 84 unicorns,

00:01:08.525 --> 00:01:13.735
Israel was one of the most advanced
technological ecosystems on the planet,

00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:17.118
and had earned the nickname
of Start-Up Nation.

00:01:19.298 --> 00:01:24.176
But it wasn't all great,
Start Up nation was in danger,

00:01:24.176 --> 00:01:27.029
one of our speakers informed us.

00:01:27.029 --> 00:01:31.463
She presented us with this report put
together by the Israeli innovation

00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:34.442
authority that stated
that at any given moment,

00:01:34.442 --> 00:01:38.732
there were over 15,000 job openings and
technical startups and

00:01:38.732 --> 00:01:43.474
tech companies, and that those companies
are just struggling to fill them.

00:01:43.474 --> 00:01:49.353
This was huge technology is by far
Israel's greatest economic driver.

00:01:49.353 --> 00:01:53.809
And now it was at a danger of hitting
a glass ceiling because of a shortage and

00:01:53.809 --> 00:01:54.600
engineers.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:02.549
The next day, I went on my first
visit to a Palestinian city.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:03.782
As an Israeli citizen,

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:07.619
I'm not allowed to go into Palestinian
cities without a special permit.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:11.870
And I could feel the tension
building in my body

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:16.017
as we made it into
the unfamiliar territory.

00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:21.040
Had a lot of preconceptions about
what the city might look like,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.999
how hostile it may feel.

00:02:25.287 --> 00:02:29.362
Those are all shattered to soon as he made
it into the beautiful city of Rawabi.

00:02:29.362 --> 00:02:33.250
The heart of the Palestinians Tech
sector that happens to

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.870
be just a little over an hour's drive
from the home that I grew up in.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:43.084
In Rawabi, we were greeted by a panel of
engineers that told us that every year

00:02:43.084 --> 00:02:48.302
3000 Palestinian software engineers
graduated into the labor market,

00:02:48.302 --> 00:02:51.432
but that over 90% of
them were unable to find

00:02:51.432 --> 00:02:54.905
jobs in the Steel Nathan Palestinian
tech sector.

00:02:57.373 --> 00:03:02.307
I looked at my colleagues,
were they hearing this?

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:07.339
A shortage of 15,000 engineers
in Israeli companies,

00:03:07.339 --> 00:03:12.661
and an hour away thousands of
Palestinians engineers looking for

00:03:12.661 --> 00:03:16.064
jobs, could these pieces be connected?

00:03:16.064 --> 00:03:20.581
I certainly thought that they could,
in fact I was so convinced that I started

00:03:20.581 --> 00:03:25.180
Tech Bridge, an organization that
connected Israeli and Palestinian tech.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.708
We worked with Israeli tech companies,
with job openings and

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:34.682
we encourage them to fill those
openings with Palestinian talent.

00:03:34.682 --> 00:03:38.906
Some were wary,
they were just convinced that employing

00:03:38.906 --> 00:03:42.077
Palestinian engineers is not a good idea.

00:03:42.077 --> 00:03:44.013
But most were simply excited,

00:03:44.013 --> 00:03:48.778
they had no idea that there were
Palestinian software engineers looking for

00:03:48.778 --> 00:03:53.033
