00:04:49.716 --> 00:04:53.301
And we are already seeing
X Kratos employees going and

00:04:53.301 --> 00:04:58.402
starting their own ventures, fueling
the Palestinian tech ecosystems and

00:04:58.402 --> 00:05:02.643
creating new jobs, and
hopefully this is just the beginning.

00:05:02.643 --> 00:05:07.193
Now there's so much more that I would
love to tell you about the challenges and

00:05:07.193 --> 00:05:09.016
opportunities in this space.

00:05:09.016 --> 00:05:16.669
But the next few minutes, I want to share
with you what excites me most about it.

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:21.157
So first, I'm excited about
Palestinian software engineers

00:05:21.157 --> 00:05:23.952
working with Israeli tech companies,

00:05:23.952 --> 00:05:28.960
because it's simply an obvious
market solution to a market problem.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.342
Has incredible positive externalities,
but at its core,

00:05:33.342 --> 00:05:37.820
it's business driven,
which ensures its organic growth.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:42.197
You have a demand for
engineers on the Israeli side, and

00:05:42.197 --> 00:05:47.891
you have a supply of engineers looking for
jobs on the Palestinian side.

00:05:47.891 --> 00:05:51.606
We've all learned in
introductory microeconomics,

00:05:51.606 --> 00:05:57.431
barring structural barriers, market forces
will lead these two into equilibrium.

00:05:57.431 --> 00:06:02.053
In other words, it just makes business
sense to match Palestinian software

00:06:02.053 --> 00:06:05.464
engineers looking for
jobs with Israeli tech company.

00:06:08.418 --> 00:06:14.509
The second reason that I'm excited about
this space is because it's a rare instance

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:20.341
where tangible action does not benefit one
side at the expense of the other side,

00:06:20.341 --> 00:06:26.625
but rather creates a win-win situation
benefiting both Israelis and Palestinians.

00:06:26.625 --> 00:06:31.469
And increasing economic prosperity
in the region as a whole.

00:06:31.469 --> 00:06:36.000
So instead of dividing the pie like in so
many other instances related to

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.468
Israel Palestinian relations,
we're actually enlarging the pie.

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:47.938
And finally, the third reason that
I'm excited about this space,

00:06:47.938 --> 00:06:52.822
is that it's simply an opportunity for
us to get to know each other.

00:06:52.822 --> 00:06:57.995
As Israelis,
many of us have never met a Palestinian.

00:06:57.995 --> 00:07:03.683
And when we hear the word Palestinian,
it's often connected with violence.

00:07:03.683 --> 00:07:08.453
And many Palestinians have only
seen Israeli soldiers would they

00:07:08.453 --> 00:07:11.145
